window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-088c850cc2afde61"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"model-selection\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">模型选择</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"meet-the-models\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">了解各个模型</h2>  <p>不同产品和模型版本的可用性、工具、推理设置和用量限制各不相同。请查看 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">ChatGPT 中可用的模型</a>或 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 模型目录</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"find-the-right-model-for-your-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">为你的工作流程选择合适的模型</h2> <p>选择你的工作类型和任务，获取模型建议。</p>  <p><a id=\"when-to-consider-gpt-61-sol\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">何时考虑 GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>如果成本也需要考虑，可在复杂项目中考虑 GPT-6.1 Sol，例如根据财务结果制作董事会演示文稿，或根据产品简介构建网站。你可以让 Astra 和 GPT-6.1 Sol 使用同一任务进行比较，从而评估质量与成本之间的取舍。</p> <p>模型规格和 API 价格请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 模型页面</a>；要了解 ChatGPT 套餐是否可使用 Codex 和 ChatGPT Work 中的该模型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">可用性说明</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-think-about-models-and-reasoning-effort\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">如何理解模型和推理强度</h2> <p>Luna 是我们的高效率模型；Astra 则是最先进、能力最强的模型。如果你不需要考虑用量或完成任务所需时间，可以默认使用 Astra。若想优化用量，请按照下面的指引选择适合需求的模型和推理强度。</p> <ol> <li><strong>Luna · Low</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于精细编辑、范围明确的问题解决和简单的信息提取。</p> <ol> <li><strong>Luna · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于跨多个应用寻找当前上下文、确定优先级，以及在明确约束下解决问题。</p> <ol> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol · Medium</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于复杂技术工作，以及需要协调、且预期会修改完善的交付成果。</p> <ol> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于精心打磨的交付成果、相互关联的视觉系统，以及需要依据相互矛盾证据作出的决策。</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Low</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于简洁写作和内容改写，同时保留事实和细微差别。</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Medium</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于需要广泛上下文、可靠交互和完整结果的复杂项目。</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>适用于要求很高的分析和复杂交付任务。</p> <p><a id=\"experiment\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">试着比较</h3> <p>把本页的建议当作起点。要找到适合自己工作流程的模型和推理设置，最好的方法是亲自试用、观察结果。</p> <p>开始时可以考虑：</p> <ul> <li><strong>工作流程运行得有多频繁？</strong> 自动化任务运行得越频繁，用量和成本累积得越快；偶尔执行则影响较小。</li> <li><strong>你需要多快拿到结果？</strong> 如果你正在等待结果，可能需要选择更快的设置；如果任务可以运行一整夜，则可以选择较慢的设置。</li> <li><strong>你准备如何使用输出？</strong> 供你检查的草稿，可能不需要像对外分享的内容那样精致。</li> <li><strong>结果质量有多重要？</strong> 视用途或行业而定，你可能希望选用更强的模型来提高质量。</li> </ul> <p>如果条件允许，请使用相同输入进行比较，并选择能达到质量要求的最轻量设置。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"model-selection\">Model selection</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"meet-the-models\">Meet the models</h2>  <p>Availability, tools, reasoning settings, and usage limits differ by product and model version. Check the <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">models available in ChatGPT</a> or the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API model catalog</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"find-the-right-model-for-your-workflow\">Find the right model for your workflow</h2> <p>Choose your work and task and get a recommendation.</p>  <h3 id=\"when-to-consider-gpt-61-sol\">When to consider GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>Consider GPT-6.1 Sol for complex projects where cost matters, such as creating a board presentation from financial results or building a website from a product brief. Compare it with Astra on the same task to assess the tradeoff between quality and cost.</p> <p>See the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API model page</a> for specifications and API pricing, or <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">Codex and ChatGPT Work availability</a> for access through your ChatGPT plan.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-think-about-models-and-reasoning-effort\">How to think about models and reasoning effort</h2> <p>Luna is our most efficient model, while Astra is our state-of-the-art, most powerful model. If you don't need to think about usage or how long it takes to complete a task, you can default to Astra. To optimize usage, use the guidance below to choose a model and reasoning effort for your needs.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Luna · Low</strong></li> </ol> <p>Fine-grained edits, well-scoped problem-solving, and simple data extraction.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Luna · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>Finding current context across multiple apps, prioritizing work, and solving problems with clear constraints.</p> <ol> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol · Medium</strong></li> </ol> <p>Complex technical work and coordinated deliverables you expect to revise.</p> <ol> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>Polished deliverables, connected visual systems, and decisions built from conflicting evidence.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Low</strong></li> </ol> <p>Concise writing and content adaptation that preserve facts and nuance.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Medium</strong></li> </ol> <p>Ambitious projects that need broad context, reliable interactions, and complete results.</p> <ol> <li><strong>Astra · Extra high</strong></li> </ol> <p>Demanding analysis and complex deliverables with exacting requirements.</p> <h3 id=\"experiment\">Experiment</h3> <p>Treat the guidance on this page as a starting point. The best way to find the right model for your workflow is to experiment with different models and reasoning settings to see what works.</p> <p>Start by considering:</p> <ul> <li><strong>How often does your workflow run?</strong> A frequent automation makes usage and cost add up faster than an occasional project.</li> <li><strong>How quickly do you need the result?</strong> A task you're waiting on may need a faster setting than one that runs overnight.</li> <li><strong>How will you use the output?</strong> A draft for your review may need less polish than something you'll share externally.</li> <li><strong>How important is the quality of the result?</strong> Depending on your use case or industry, you might want to use a stronger model to put an emphasis on quality.</li> </ul> <p>If you can, experiment using the same inputs to compare results and keep the lightest setting that meets your quality bar.</p>"};
